1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,762
Minimalism: Less Is More.

2
00:00:02,712 --> 00:00:06,300
Minimalism is not about owning as little as possible.

3
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:09,537
It is about intentionality with possessions.

4
00:00:09,537 --> 00:00:14,100
Physical clutter competes for attention and creates low-grade stress.

5
00:00:14,100 --> 00:00:18,987
Research indicates that people with cluttered homes have higher cortisol levels.

6
00:00:18,987 --> 00:00:21,900
Decluttering frees mental bandwidth.

7
00:00:21,900 --> 00:00:27,437
Before acquiring something new, the minimalist asks whether it will genuinely add value.

8
00:00:27,437 --> 00:00:31,487
The same principle applies to commitments and digital consumption.

9
00:00:31,487 --> 00:00:34,200
Minimalism is not deprivation.

10
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:39,312
It is making space, literally and psychologically, for what matters most.

